<%# watch-list-swap.ejs
     What comes back when you hold, resume or delete a watch.

     Holding a watch used to reload the page: a POST, a redirect, a fresh
     document, three stylesheets and every query behind the topbar, to
     change one word on one button. This sends the list, and the three
     things elsewhere on the page that the change actually invalidates.

     The rows replace the target. The three shell readouts ride out of
     band, which is the only honest way to do it: they are real
     consequences of the mutation, not decoration. Left stale they show
     "2/2 watches, sweeping" over a list where one is plainly held, and
     a sidebar tally of 1 over an empty list. %>
<%- include('./watch-rows', { watches, csrfToken, tprFor, rel, sourceLabel }) %>
<span class="dot <%= activeCount ? 'live' : 'off' %>" id="watchPanelDot" hx-swap-oob="true"></span>
<%- include('./readouts', { oob: true, sweeping, watchCount, activeCount, nextSweepAt }) %>
<%- include('./nav-count', { oob: true, watchCount }) %>
